{=============================================================================
  R113 power-to-power ratio of an ORC and a heat pump
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0229
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Teaching example of ULiège MECA0002 (August 2022). The ratio is the
  turbine AC electrical power over the compressor AC electrical power.
  The turbine uses a given enthalpy drop of 17.5 kJ/kg. The compressor
  uses the saturated evaporator exit and a condenser inlet superheated
  by 5 C. Mechanical efficiency 97 %, converter efficiency 92 %. The
  stated 89 % isentropic efficiency is not written as an equation.
  Compressor inlet and outlet only: no diagram-state arrays.

  Inputs : m_dot_orc, m_dot_pac, delta_h_turb, p1, p3, eta_meca, eta_conv
  Outputs: Power_to_power_ratio, W_cp, W_turb_fluide_elec
  Units  : SI - temperatures in K, pressures in Pa, energies in J
           (property calls receive °C)
  Source : ULiège MECA0002, Q5_power_to_power_ratio.EES; the equation
           window names no author - see README.md
  Licence: MIT. Status: verified against the EES stored solution.
=============================================================================}

"!Problem"
"Teaching example, as in the original. The ORC turbine has an isentropic efficiency of 89 % and the fluid enthalpy changes by 17.5 kJ/kg. The ORC refrigerant flow is 1.2 kg/s."
"The power-to-power ratio is the absolute value of the turbine AC electrical power over the compressor AC electrical power, as in the original."
"The compressor is driven by an electric motor through a converter. The turbine drives a generator through a mechanical link and a converter, as in the original."
"The mechanical efficiency of each link is 97 %. The converter efficiency is 92 %, as in the original."
"The heat-pump fluid flow is 200 g/s. The evaporator and condenser pressures are 45 kPa and 320 kPa, as in the original."
"The fluid is superheated by 5 C at the condenser inlet. At the evaporator outlet (compressor inlet) the fluid is saturated, as in the original."

"!Given data"
m_dot_orc = 1.2 [kg/s]                                    "ORC refrigerant mass flow [kg/s], as in the original"
m_dot_pac = 0.2 [kg/s]                                    "heat-pump fluid mass flow [kg/s], 200 g/s as in the original"
delta_h_turb = 17.5*1000 [J/kg]                          "turbine enthalpy drop [J/kg]; 17.5 kJ/kg written as 17.5*1000, as in the original"

p1 = 45e3 [Pa]                                            "evaporator pressure [Pa], 45 kPa written as 45e3, as in the original"
p2 = p1                                                   "compressor inlet pressure [Pa], as in the original"
p3 = 320e3 [Pa]                                           "condenser pressure [Pa], 320 kPa written as 320e3, as in the original"
p4 = p3                                                   "set equal to p3, as in the original"

"!Heat-pump compressor inlet and outlet"
"Temperatures stay in kelvin. T_sat returns °C, so 273.15 is added at the property boundary."
T2 = T_sat(R113, P=p2) + 273.15                          "saturation temperature at the compressor inlet [K]"
T_cond = T_sat(R113, P=p3) + 273.15                      "saturation temperature at the condenser pressure [K]"
T3 = T_cond + 5                                           "condenser inlet temperature [K]; superheat of 5 °C, as in the original"

h2 = enthalpy(R113, P=p2, x=1)                           "saturated vapour enthalpy at the compressor inlet [J/kg], as in the original"
h3 = enthalpy(R113, T=T3-273.15, P=p3)                   "enthalpy at the condenser inlet [J/kg]; the call takes °C and T3 is in K"

"!Efficiencies and power-to-power ratio"
eta_meca = 0.97                                           "mechanical efficiency of each link [-], as in the original"
eta_conv = 0.92                                           "converter efficiency [-], as in the original"

W_cp = abs(m_dot_pac*(h3-h2))/eta_meca/eta_conv          "compressor electrical power [W], absolute value as in the original"
W_turb_fluide = m_dot_orc*delta_h_turb                    "turbine fluid power [W], as in the original"
W_turb_fluide_elec = W_turb_fluide*eta_meca*eta_conv      "turbine electrical power [W], as in the original"
Power_to_power_ratio = W_turb_fluide_elec/W_cp            "power-to-power ratio [-], as in the original"
